-- TV Shows

The narrative largely revolves around the women attempting to balance their entrepreneurial ambitions with their roles as wives, mothers, and friends. Cast members frequently launch fashion lines, beauty brands, music careers, and restaurants, often bringing them into competition or partnership with one another. Alongside their business pursuits, the series documents their domestic lives, including marriages, difficult divorces, the challenges of raising children in the spotlight, and the complex management of extended family relationships.

A central engine of the series is the constantly shifting social hierarchy among the women. They regularly gather for lavish parties, charity galas, and domestic vacations, as well as highly produced cast trips to international destinations. These gatherings serve as the primary stage for both deep bonding and intense interpersonal conflict, where misunderstandings, rumors, and perceived slights frequently escalate into long-standing feuds. Rivalries naturally form and dissolve, with alliances shifting from season to season based on loyalty, business disputes, or personal betrayals. At the conclusion of each season, the cast convenes for a multi-part reunion special to discuss the preceding events, air out their grievances, and attempt to resolve conflicts under the moderation of the network, setting the stage for the social dynamics of the following year.', '["background noise for folding an insurmountable pile of laundry","a stark reminder of why gossip is a sin","grown adults completely failing at basic conflict resolution","women wearing evening gowns to daytime events"]', 'Returning Series', 'Bravo', 'Georgia peaches with a side of drama.', 5.9, 123, '2008-10-07', '2025-07-27', 17.8815, 'en', 'The Real Housewives of Atlanta', 'http://www.bravotv.com/the-real-housewives-of-atlanta', 352, 17, 1, 'Reality', 'US', '/h5HYOsyc1sJQYjqevaWEaLRjd6E.jpg', '/1FygXfA7eqGrd1sDENLtvgAVaNb.jpg', '2026-04-03T16:34:44Z', '2026-04-03T19:35:20Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

The episodes follow a strict weekly schedule based on the bus''s destination. On Mondays, the bus arrives at the Why Bird Stop, set in a bustling Lost Property Office. Here, the inquisitive puppet Why Bird interacts with a human bus driver to file unclaimed items, often using a special computer to discover facts, play videos, and solve problems. Tuesdays feature the Playground Stop, where presenters lead groups of children in energetic activities, games, and crafts. This stop also regularly includes a segment with a singing marionette named Lizzie Dreams and incorporates Makaton sign language into its rhymes. Wednesdays bring the bus to the Dot Stop—later revamped as the Roundabout Stop—which focuses on music, rhythm, and counting, often guided by characters like Mr. Jolly, Bitsy Bob, and various musical puppets.

On Thursdays, the bus pulls into the Patch Stop, an adventure-based segment initially centered around a gentle scarecrow doll named Sam Patch. He is later succeeded by a rag doll named Peggy Patch, who travels to real-world locations, leaving picture clues for children to find her. Fridays feature the Tent Stop, where actors and children collaborate to dress up and perform theatrical plays, often utilizing a magical chest of costumes. This stop later evolves into the Poppy Stop, set at the house of a feline puppet named Poppy, where various characters gather for stories and songs. Throughout the series, the program emphasizes active participation and inclusivity, stepping away from the traditional direct-to-camera presentation style to create a dynamic, varied learning environment for preschoolers.', '["television that assumes children have an attention span","gentle programming to lower the household blood pressure","puppets who are just trying to do their jobs","british people being relentlessly cheerful"]', 'Ended', 'BBC One', '', 6.5, 4, '1988-10-17', '1988-10-17', 0.3883, 'en', 'Playdays', '', 1, 1, 0, 'Scripted', 'GB', NULL, NULL, '2026-04-03T17:20:34Z', '2026-04-03T19:35:52Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

The series operates as a televised storybook, treating legendary folklore with a blend of earnest reverence and playful, tongue-in-cheek humor. Throughout its run, the show brings familiar narratives to life, ranging from "Rumpelstiltskin" and "Cinderella" to "The Snow Queen" and "The Pied Piper of Hamelin". The production is notable for its star-studded ensemble casts and prominent guest directors, merging Hollywood talent with traditional storytelling. Famous actors frequently take on iconic roles, such as Robin Williams as the Frog Prince, Susan Sarandon as Beauty, Christopher Reeve as Prince Charming, and Joan Collins as the wicked witch in "Hansel and Gretel".

Rather than relying on modern special effects, the series emphasizes theatrical artifice, utilizing early video effects, rich musical scores, and stageplay aesthetics. The adaptations balance moral lessons and dramatic tension with lighthearted whimsy, ensuring the stories appeal to both children and adults. By preserving the original narrative arcs of classic fairy tales—where virtue is rewarded, vanity is punished, and courage overcomes dark magic—the series celebrates the enduring imaginative power of foundational folklore.', '["a-list celebrities taking children''s theater extremely seriously","magical worlds built entirely out of cardboard and earnestness","storybook adaptations that trust children with actual vocabulary","watching this feels like staying home sick from school"]', 'Ended', 'Showtime', '26 ways to live happily ever after.', 8.1, 23, '1982-09-11', '1987-11-14', 19.2378, 'en', 'Faerie Tale Theatre', '', 27, 6, 0, 'Scripted', 'US', '/5pKkikAvKfyiAmxwkw1HHb2z2Za.jpg', '/3aNOOw4jZwv2gqwDqlZLqaAvOyr.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:38:40Z', '2026-04-03T19:36:00Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

Dudley is a happy-go-lucky figure whose innocence frequently requires him to learn basic moral and practical lessons from his human companions. He maintains an affinity for "dragonberries" and his treasured stuffed animal, Freddy Bear. As the series progresses, the core cast expands to include other neighborhood children—such as Terry, Julia, Mickey, and Laura—who step in to assist Dudley in his daily exploits. They are joined by a colorful supporting cast of forest-dwelling creatures and eccentric locals represented through both costumed actors and hand puppets. These include Sammy, a laid-back frog; a family of anthropomorphic Robins; a lovable Caveman who eventually overcomes his bullying tendencies to become a loyal friend; and Mr. Crabby Tree, a grouchy but wise apple tree who occasionally uses his magical roots to interact with the forest ecosystem.

The show''s narrative is episodic, generally focusing on gentle, low-stakes dilemmas such as localized pollution, minor interpersonal misunderstandings, or Dudley''s confusion over human holidays and traditions. Occasionally, the ensemble must deal with more prominent nuisances, such as a mischievous leprechaun, a genie who encourages the wasteful use of energy, or a toxic specter haunting Dudley''s cave. Despite his willingness to explore, Dudley''s adventures frequently reinforce his appreciation for the safety of his cave and the stability of his found family. The overarching narrative culminates in the series finale when Dudley confronts the possibility that he is the last of his kind. He embarks on a quest to find another living dragon, but ultimately concludes that his human and animal companions are his true family, just before a brief encounter hints that other dragons still quietly exist in the world.', '["children patiently explaining how the world works to magical creatures","adults in unventilated foam suits teaching basic virtues","gentle television that lowers your heart rate","low stakes problems resolved by simply apologizing"]', 'Ended', 'YTV', '', 10.0, 1, '1993-10-08', '1993-10-08', 1.4497, 'en', 'The Adventures of Dudley the Dragon', '', 65, 5, 0, 'Scripted', 'CA', '/vcXy5sUiMYDxZkBxKdiocgEXZt3.jpg', '/8eMuGZWoRmEWBu5viWo1PrkXLlX.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:12:13Z', '2026-04-03T19:36:29Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

The series is divided into eight stories that chronicle the daily lives and adventures of the hedge''s residents. Throughout the year, the mice organize elaborate seasonal festivals, such as building a grand ice palace for the midwinter Snow Ball, planning a surprise spring birthday picnic for young Wilfred Toadflax, and preparing for the summer river-raft wedding of Poppy Eyebright and Dusty Dogwood. Meanwhile, the energetic and curious youngsters, Wilfred and Primrose Woodmouse, frequently seek out adventure. Their explorations lead them to get lost in the uncharted wilderness during the autumn blackberry harvest, and later to discover a hidden labyrinth of abandoned rooms and a secret staircase within the Old Oak Palace while practicing a poem for the midwinter celebrations.

As the community grows, the mice undertake broader expeditions beyond the hedge. Wilfred joins Mr. Apple on a trek into the High Hills in search of legendary treasure, while Dusty and Poppy lead a sailing journey downriver to Seagull Rock to trade for salt with the sea mice. Ultimately, the community rallies to prepare a surprise new home for Poppy and Dusty''s expanding family, culminating in a joyous naming day ceremony for their newborn babies.', '["makes you want to abandon modern society and live in a hollowed out tree","low stakes adventures where no one gets eaten","married couples who genuinely enjoy each other''s company","someone cooks and your whole nervous system resets"]', 'Ended', 'BBC One', '', 7.0, 1, '1996-12-25', '2000-01-03', 2.7613, 'en', 'The Enchanted World of Brambly Hedge', '', 8, 1, 0, 'Scripted', 'US,GB', '/vqn0Hhw76xGtQb6FOnvSXi1qRue.jpg', '/5Lb6W2cw4sdlMqdb7wB4pcVk2uP.jpg', '2026-04-03T16:14:05Z', '2026-04-03T19:36:28Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

Throughout its run, the series explores the emotional and practical challenges of childhood from a kid''s perspective. Storylines frequently revolve around school projects, playground disputes, sibling rivalries, and the anxieties of growing up. While early seasons focus heavily on common childhood experiences like losing baby teeth, getting glasses, or avoiding the strict school bullies, later seasons gradually introduce more complex issues such as dyslexia, asthma, and Asperger''s syndrome. Despite the evolving subject matter, the narrative maintains a grounded, slice-of-life approach, emphasizing the importance of honesty, empathy, and working through mistakes. The kids frequently rely on their imaginations to solve problems, often daydreaming in exaggerated scenarios before coming to realistic resolutions within their community.', '["unapologetic library card propaganda","kids treating minor inconveniences like greek tragedies","the anxiety of seeing your teacher at the grocery store","siblings who genuinely act like siblings"]', 'Ended', 'PBS', 'What a wonderful kind of day!', 7.0, 176, '1996-10-07', '2022-02-21', 23.3651, 'en', 'Arthur', 'http://www.pbskids.org/arthur/', 493, 25, 0, 'Scripted', 'US,CA', '/nYN8okmcsmhd4bGVcqifZ5OCumB.jpg', '/5k3JpB88vubqYVSHHiAhk2T8z17.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:37:54Z', '2026-04-03T19:37:02Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

Each episode centers on the staff''s interactions with these customers, blending historical education with the art of negotiation. When presented with unique artifacts—ranging from Revolutionary War documents and antique firearms to classic cars and pop culture memorabilia—the Harrisons examine the items and discuss their historical context. Because of the vast diversity and potential high value of the objects, Rick and the team frequently call upon a trusted network of local experts, including historians, restorers, and appraisers, to authenticate the items and determine their true market value. Once an item is authenticated, the Harrisons engage in spirited haggling with the seller, always aiming to secure a price that allows the shop to turn a profit while factoring in potential restoration and auction costs.

Beyond the buying and selling of historical artifacts, the series highlights the interpersonal dynamics and comedic camaraderie among the shop''s staff. Storylines frequently revolve around the generational clashes between the Harrisons. The Old Man routinely enforces strict business standards and shares wisdom from his younger days, often reprimanding the staff for being lazy. Rick acts as the knowledgeable and shrewd driving force of the business, frequently mediating between his father and his son. Corey strives to prove his business acumen and earn a larger stake in the company, while Chumlee provides comic relief through his perceived incompetence, endearing missteps, and occasional surprising areas of expertise. These internal conflicts, practical jokes, and friendly wagers form the backdrop to the shop''s daily grind, capturing the tension and humor of running a high-stakes family business. In later seasons, the format expands to include the crew traveling to various cities across the country to meet fans and acquire rare items on the road.', '["men looking at old objects and nodding gravely","background noise for folding laundry","dads turning every conversation into a history lecture","family businesses held together by sarcasm and sheer willpower"]', 'Returning Series', 'History', '', 7.122, 295, '2009-07-19', '2026-03-18', 19.8833, 'en', 'Pawn Stars', 'http://www.history.com/shows/pawn-stars', 680, 24, 1, 'Reality', 'US', '/3YxmQmoSbv9bXHYWIEDztstZguC.jpg', '/zzZzApaNDa2IxQUWo8x3Rbgs7iW.jpg', '2026-04-03T16:34:15Z', '2026-04-03T19:37:07Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

Ned''s death triggers the War of the Five Kings. His eldest son, Robb, is declared King in the North, while Robert''s brothers Stannis and Renly each claim the Iron Throne. Balon Greyjoy also declares independence for the Iron Islands. As the war ravages Westeros, the wealthy Lannister family manages to maintain control of the throne through strategic alliances, ultimately orchestrating the brutal massacre of Robb and Catelyn Stark at the Red Wedding. Meanwhile, across the Narrow Sea in Essos, Daenerys Targaryen, the exiled daughter of the dynasty deposed by King Robert, rises to power. Initially sold into marriage with Dothraki warlord Khal Drogo, Daenerys survives his death and miraculously hatches three dragons. Over several seasons, she conquers the cities of Slaver''s Bay, emancipates their slaves, and amasses a massive army of Unsullied and Dothraki warriors to reclaim the Iron Throne.

Simultaneously, a supernatural threat emerges in the icy lands north of the Wall, a massive ice structure protected by the Night''s Watch. Ned Stark''s illegitimate son, Jon Snow, joins the order and quickly rises through its ranks. Jon discovers that the White Walkers, an ancient army of the undead led by the Night King, are marching on the realms of men. To combat this existential threat, Jon forms an uneasy alliance with the wildlings who live beyond the Wall and eventually reaches out to Daenerys Targaryen when she finally lands her forces in Westeros.

After Cersei Lannister violently eliminates her rivals in King''s Landing and seizes the Iron Throne for herself, Jon and Daenerys temporarily suspend the war for the throne to confront the Night King. The combined armies of the living meet the army of the dead at the Battle of Winterfell, culminating in the Night King''s destruction and the eradication of the White Walkers. With the northern threat neutralized, Daenerys turns her attention back to King''s Landing. Despite the city''s surrender, a grief-stricken and increasingly ruthless Daenerys uses her last surviving dragon to burn King''s Landing to the ground, massacring its inhabitants. Recognizing that her tyrannical vision of a new world will only bring more destruction, Jon Snow assassinates Daenerys. In the aftermath, the surviving lords and ladies of Westeros elect Bran Stark, Ned''s paralyzed and mystically gifted son, as the new King of the Six Kingdoms. The North is granted independence under Queen Sansa Stark, while Jon Snow is exiled back to the Night''s Watch.', '["people who desperately need a good confession","the map at the beginning is not optional","makes your family thanksgiving look completely functional","absolutely no one needed to die but here we are"]', 'Ended', 'HBO', 'Winter is coming.', 8.459, 26538, '2011-04-17', '2019-05-19', 194.3937, 'en', 'Game of Thrones', 'https://www.hbo.com/game-of-thrones', 73, 8, 0, 'Scripted', 'US', '/1XS1oqL89opfnbLl8WnZY1O1uJx.jpg', '/zZqpAXxVSBtxV9qPBcscfXBcL2w.jpg', '2026-04-03T15:40:34Z', '2026-04-03T19:37:44Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

Returning to the garden night after night, Tom finds he has slipped back in time to the 1880s. He is invisible to the household''s inhabitants, save for Hatty, an orphaned girl who lives as a poor relation with her cruel aunt and older cousins. Both lonely in their respective times, Tom and Hatty form a deep friendship and share numerous adventures in the grounds of the estate. However, Tom soon realizes that time in the garden moves strangely; while he remains the same age, Hatty grows rapidly older with each visit, transitioning from a young girl into a young woman of the Victorian era.

As Tom''s quarantine nears its end, he desperately seeks a way to stay in the garden forever. When he attempts to visit on his final night, he finds the garden door has vanished, leaving only the grim modern yard. The next day, Tom finally meets Mrs. Bartholomew and discovers that she is the elderly Hatty. The magical midnight garden was a manifestation of her vivid dreams and fondest childhood memories, which Tom''s own loneliness allowed him to enter. Recognizing each other across the gulf of time, the two share a poignant reunion before Tom returns home to his family.', '["getting stuck with boring relatives and finding magic in the backyard","clocks behaving suspiciously","friendships that make you inexplicably sad about the passage of time","elderly characters quietly carrying the entire emotional payload"]', 'Ended', 'BBC One', '', 6.0, 1, '1989-01-04', '1989-02-08', 0.9666, 'en', 'Tom''s Midnight Garden', '', 6, 1, 0, 'Miniseries', 'GB', '/fCJa3Bz9eOZzk9Epv39RAZG6Pp9.jpg', '/AkoIioePKwDMfFY4ib3n0LAZ9ZA.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:17:52Z', '2026-04-03T19:37:48Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

The overarching narrative faithfully mirrors Alexandre Dumas''s classic adventure, transforming the historical epic into a family-friendly tale of loyalty, bravery, and chivalry. As Dogtanian adjusts to life in Paris, he becomes entangled in dangerous political intrigue. The heroes must constantly thwart the insidious machinations of the power-hungry Cardinal Richelieu, who seeks to undermine the King and seize control of France. Richelieu''s efforts are enforced by his ruthless captain of the guards, Rochefort, and his stealthy, calculating feline spy, Milady de Winter.

Amidst the constant threat of espionage and sword fights, Dogtanian falls deeply in love with Juliette, a devoted maid-in-waiting to Queen Anne. A major narrative arc involves Dogtanian and the Muskehounds embarking on a perilous journey to England to recover the Queen''s diamond studs, racing against time and Richelieu''s agents to protect her honor and prevent an international incident. Accompanied by his clever mouse sidekick, Pip, who often scouts ahead and provides crucial distractions, Dogtanian learns the value of discipline, sacrifice, and true friendship. Across the series, the plucky young swordsman continuously risks his life for his friends and his country, ultimately striving to prove his courage and earn his rightful place as an official member of the King''s guard.', '["classic literature filtered entirely through animated animals","young men leaving home with a sword and absolutely zero life experience","friendships so earnest they make modern cynicism look deeply embarrassing","rodent sidekicks doing the heavy lifting","swordplay with an aggressively strict moral code"]', 'Ended', 'MBS', '', 7.307, 70, '1981-10-09', '1982-03-26', 5.9953, 'es', 'D''Artacán y los tres mosqueperros', 'https://brb.es/en/dartacan-y-los-tres-mosqueperros', 26, 1, 0, 'Miniseries', 'JP,ES', '/rHFBZgPpgHIXFz1jP5xdZlkmPqu.jpg', '/juEqGPmRFYd5iBGS4ID2qOnXPv9.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:18:42Z', '2026-04-03T19:37:58Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

Upon settling in the reserve, the Farthing Wood animals face new challenges. The resident animals are not entirely welcoming, and Fox finds himself in a bitter territorial rivalry with Scarface, a vicious blue fox with a vendetta against the newcomers. The second major arc focuses on the animals adapting to their new environment, enduring a harsh winter, and dealing with internal conflicts as well as the temptation of predators to break the Oath. The feud between the red and blue foxes escalates into a brutal war, culminating in Scarface''s defeat and the gradual integration of the Farthing Wood animals into the wider community of the park.

In the final arc, a massive swarm of aggressive rats, led by the tyrannical Bully, invades White Deer Park, threatening to consume all resources and drive the other animals out. The aging Farthing Wood originals and their offspring must unite with the park''s native inhabitants to repel the rodent army. As the older generation of animals, including Fox and his mate, begin to pass away from old age, the younger generation steps up to lead and defend their home. The animals successfully defeat the rats, ensuring the survival and legacy of the Farthing Wood community in their hard-won sanctuary.', '["childrens animation that absolutely refuses to sugarcoat mortality","environmental destruction viewed entirely through the eyes of stressed woodland creatures","walking an unfathomable distance because your home was destroyed","taking a solemn vow to not eat your traveling companions"]', 'Ended', 'BBC One', '', 8.245, 55, '1993-01-03', '1995-12-21', 3.3155, 'en', 'The Animals of Farthing Wood', '', 39, 3, 0, 'Scripted', 'GB', '/aRKM4v1j46jxtHR3wfbNTUrYg0T.jpg', '/u8hU5zQ16Mg0qNwp0FgolTVo99H.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:18:48Z', '2026-04-03T19:38:11Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

Each episode centers around a specific wildlife theme, such as animal families, defense mechanisms, or unique habitats. Zoboo typically introduces the theme by describing a mystery animal he encountered on his way to the junction. This prompts the Who Could It Be segment, an animated sequence where the brothers attempt to guess the animal''s identity based on Zoboo''s clues. The mystery is resolved when the actual animal arrives at Animal Junction, allowing the hosts to examine its behaviors and adaptations up close.

The central live-action explorations are interspersed with various recurring segments. Throughout the episode, Zoboo shares stories from Zobooland, an imaginative stop-motion claymation world populated by mythical, colorful creatures like Gooble and Narchi. The Kratt brothers also frequently leave Animal Junction to embark on field expeditions, traveling across the globe to observe creatures in their natural habitats. Along the way, the series highlights the Animal Helpers, segments featuring real children who demonstrate how to care for pets and protect local wildlife. Through interactive play, original songs, and physical comedy, the hosts bridge the gap between human environments and the animal kingdom, culminating in a farewell song as Zoboo returns to his home in Madagascar and the visitors depart Animal Junction.', '["people in cargo shorts being extremely enthusiastic about nature","brothers who genuinely enjoy each other''s company","the undeniable urge to go outside and find a bug","shows that make you want to adopt a creature you are not equipped to handle"]', 'Ended', 'TVOntario', '', 6.7, 33, '1999-01-25', '2001-06-07', 7.2549, 'en', 'Zoboomafoo', 'http://www.pbs.org/zoboo', 65, 2, 0, 'Scripted', 'CA,US', '/5JMgrHBaspcU9KIfC7nTfPFNL9x.jpg', '/OMZrF60GxJa1iUA78SwwRDjd0k.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:10:54Z', '2026-04-03T19:38:30Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

Ivor''s world is rooted in the close-knit community of Grumbly and the surrounding valleys. The railway operates under the strict but benevolent eye of Dai Station, the local stationmaster who often finds himself exasperated by the engine''s eccentricities but remains fiercely protective of the line. Over the course of the series, Ivor engages in various community activities that go far beyond pulling passenger coaches and freight. In an early storyline, Ivor discovers a deep love for choral music. After being fitted with three pipes from a fairground organ, he successfully auditions to sing first bass in the Grumbly and District Choral Society, directed by the enthusiastic choirmaster Evans the Song.

The series blends mundane rural chores with elements of quiet fantasy. One of the primary ongoing storylines involves the discovery of Idris, a small, fire-breathing Welsh dragon who hatches from an egg found in Ivor''s firebox. Idris eventually takes up residence inside the furnace, keeping Ivor''s boiler hot while the dragon''s family settles in an extinct local volcano. Ivor and his human companions frequently band together to protect Idris and the other dragons from outside interference, such as the prying eyes of an antiquarian society.

Other recurring misadventures involve rescuing stranded sheep, running errands for the locals, delivering fish and tomatoes, and dealing with deep winter snowdrifts. Ivor frequently socializes with his best friend, a donkey named Bluebell, and crosses paths with a variety of eccentric community members, including the upper-class animal lover Mrs. Porty and the inventive gold prospector Mr. Dinwiddy. Whether he is transporting a lost circus elephant or helping his neighbors overcome small, everyday crises, Ivor''s actions are driven by his distinct personality and his deep bond with Jones the Steam, who treats the little engine more like a son than a machine. The series concludes with the railway and its community remaining exactly as they have always been: peaceful, cooperative, and deeply anchored in local tradition.', '["gentle animation that resets your central nervous system","cozy british villages where the stakes are incredibly low","anthropomorphic machines with exceptional civic virtue","grown men treating small community events with the utmost seriousness"]', 'Ended', 'ITV1', '', 7.0, 3, '1976-01-26', '1977-12-23', 1.5788, 'en', 'Ivor the Engine', '', 97, 5, 0, 'Scripted', 'GB', '/79VQwrUHwmIhh50BlvUV3aqh0mb.jpg', '/8jBafwkUk3pIh8Sj1JV5LPc4hJA.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:24:24Z', '2026-04-03T19:38:50Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

The episodic storylines frequently revolve around Madeline’s impulsive curiosity, which inevitably leads to a predicament. Whether she is rescuing a stray dog named Genevieve, who becomes the school''s beloved mascot, or reforming the mischievous Spanish ambassador''s son next door, Pepito, Madeline''s bravery is always at the forefront. Pepito transitions from a bullying neighbor with a bad hat to one of Madeline''s most trusted friends, frequently joining the girls on their outings. 

Many episodes feature the girls exploring the cultural landmarks of Paris or traveling abroad to places like London and Hollywood. Along the way, they must outsmart thieves, help lost animals, and win over the stern, wealthy school trustee, Lord Cucuface. Meanwhile, Miss Clavel serves as the deeply intuitive, maternal anchor of the household. Whenever Madeline’s antics escalate, Miss Clavel inevitably bolts upright in bed with the sudden, alarming realization that something is not right, rushing to rescue her charges. Despite the frequent chaos, Madeline’s adventures always conclude with a return to the safety and structure of the old house in Paris, emphasizing the enduring bonds of friendship, the importance of compassion, and the comforting presence of a loving guardian.', '["caretakers operating entirely on adrenaline and prayer","tiny girls with an intimidating amount of self-confidence","feral neighborhood boys who just needed some grace and boundaries","the profound spiritual peace of watching children walk in a straight line"]', 'Ended', 'ABC', '', 5.7, 34, '1988-11-07', '2001-02-28', 8.873, 'en', 'Madeline', '', 65, 3, 0, 'Scripted', 'US,FR,CA', '/kh1xdNqCYj4plWOyYjSIrPzzUvI.jpg', '/kNTaLz6t7JTaRyWZXpriBg6asGn.jpg', '2026-04-03T16:34:01Z', '2026-04-03T19:38:57Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

As Geralt traverses the Continent, his destiny becomes inextricably bound to two powerful women. Yennefer of Vengerberg is a fiercely ambitious sorceress born with a physical deformity. After enduring brutal training at the magical academy of Aretuza, Yennefer undergoes a painful transformation to gain beauty and power, though at the permanent cost of her fertility. Her quest for legacy and purpose repeatedly crosses paths with Geralt, resulting in a complex but enduring bond. Meanwhile, the young Crown Princess Cirilla, known as Ciri, is forced to flee her home when the expanding, militant empire of Nilfgaard brutally invades the kingdom of Cintra. Ciri possesses exceptionally potent, latent magical abilities derived from her rare Elder Blood, making her the target of multiple factions. Unbeknownst to her, she is magically tied to Geralt through the ''Law of Surprise'', an ancient custom dictating that Geralt is destined to protect her.

The series chronicles the convergence of these three disparate lives across shifting timelines. Upon finally finding Ciri, Geralt brings her to the hidden witcher fortress of Kaer Morhen, taking on the role of a surrogate father while instructing her in swordplay, resilience, and survival. Yennefer, wrestling with her own magical losses and past mistakes, eventually joins them to teach Ciri how to harness and control her immense magical potential. Together, the trio slowly forms a fragile, chosen family, providing each other with the love and belonging they have all long been denied.

However, the Continent is constantly engulfed in political machinations, racial tensions between humans and elves, and brutal wars. The Northern Kingdoms, the Nilfgaardian Empire, the renegade elves, and an otherworldly spectral army known as the Wild Hunt all seek to capture Ciri to weaponize her extraordinary abilities. Geralt and Yennefer are forced to stand together against a vast array of enemies—from power-hungry mages and treacherous spies to ancient demons. They must sacrifice their own selfish desires, embracing their parental duties to protect their surrogate daughter and maintain their familial bond amidst a broken world determined to tear them apart.', '["grumpy men who would violently defend their adopted daughters","realizing you cannot stay neutral in a fallen world","men communicating primarily through grunts and sighs","sacrificing absolutely everything to protect a child","horses that are better listeners than most humans"]', 'Returning Series', 'Netflix', 'Destiny is a beast.', 7.935, 6608, '2019-12-20', '2025-10-30', 60.1672, 'en', 'The Witcher', 'https://www.netflix.com/title/80189685', 32, 4, 1, 'Scripted', 'US', '/AoGsDM02UVt0npBA8OvpDcZbaMi.jpg', '/foGkPxpw9h8zln81j63mix5B7m8.jpg', '2026-04-03T15:40:44Z', '2026-04-03T19:39:16Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

In the second series, The Return of the Borrowers, the caretaker''s cottage is vacated, and the Clocks are once again displaced. Forced to journey through a perilous jungle of fields and rivers to find a new home, they seek out Little Fordham, a miniature model village built by a sympathetic railwayman, Mr. Pott. Along the way, they are pursued by Mild Eye, a hostile tinker, and must endure treacherous conditions. Upon reaching Little Fordham, the family briefly enjoys living in houses perfectly scaled to their size. Their peace is shattered when they are kidnapped by the greedy Platters, a couple who owns a rival model village and intends to display the tiny family for profit in a glass cage. Imprisoned in an attic, the ingenious Clocks manage to scavenge materials to construct a makeshift, candle-powered hot air balloon. They make a daring escape through an open window just as the Platters return for them. Free once more, the family sets off in a small boat down the stream, embracing their uncertain future with resilience and the knowledge that they will always find a way to survive.', '["tiny people turning literal garbage into surprisingly lovely real estate","the sheer logistical nightmare of keeping a family alive outdoors","prestigious british actors taking a children''s fantasy premise absolutely seriously","parents having a nervous breakdown because their teenager wants to go outside"]', 'Ended', 'BBC Two', '', 6.4, 11, '1992-11-08', '1993-12-19', 3.436, 'en', 'The Borrowers', '', 12, 2, 0, 'Miniseries', 'GB', '/sZaefhd3UeSeEso2rCcIPAewjDu.jpg', '/eK20eVn1JfJqUIYnrmdJfR8agHi.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:17:46Z', '2026-04-03T19:39:39Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

The series follows the team—which grows to include Jamal, Lenni, Alex, Gaby, Tina, Rob, and Hector—as they investigate local neighborhood crimes ranging from stolen backpacks and arson to computer hacking and smuggling. Because adults cannot see Ghostwriter or his messages, the kids cannot rely on supernatural proof to close a case. Instead, they must use reading comprehension, critical thinking, and traditional investigative footwork to gather tangible evidence. Ghostwriter acts as their eyes and ears across time and space, slipping under doors and into locked filing cabinets to uncover hidden documents, while relying entirely on the children to physically navigate the world and explain non-textual concepts. Across multiple multi-episode story arcs, the team navigates sibling rivalries, family expectations, and community conflicts while discovering the inherent power of language, literacy, and friendship.', '["middle schoolers with better conflict resolution skills than most adults","saving the day via intense library research","educational television that absolutely did not have to go this hard","solving neighborhood mysteries on a strict curfew"]', 'Canceled', 'BBC Two', '', 7.0, 14, '1992-10-03', '1995-02-12', 9.483, 'en', 'Ghostwriter', '', 87, 4, 0, 'Scripted', 'US,GB', '/1enj0PMkMBUtRYbWZbfsmv7DUrO.jpg', '/pRKydsDEs69Sp6rFHEKgLhoT2TJ.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:40:27Z', '2026-04-03T19:39:48Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

The series'' foundation is heavily shaped by the complex, often volatile sibling dynamic between former child actresses Kyle and Kim Richards. Their unresolved childhood traumas and Kim''s highly publicized battle with sobriety generate significant emotional friction in early seasons, culminating in legendary verbal altercations. Alongside them, imposing British restaurateur Lisa Vanderpump establishes herself as the sharp-tongued matriarch of the group, utilizing her dry wit and strategic social maneuvering to maintain control over the group''s dynamics. The initial seasons also highlight raw, surprisingly dark personal crises, most notably Taylor Armstrong''s harrowing experience with domestic abuse and her husband''s subsequent suicide, as well as Camille Grammer''s highly public divorce from actor Kelsey Grammer.

As the series progresses, the focus expands to include new dominant personalities who introduce fresh controversies. Lisa Rinna brings a soap-opera-level intensity, frequently demanding that her castmates own their mistakes while instigating massive blowups, such as a near-physical altercation during a cast trip to Amsterdam and a prolonged investigation into Yolanda Hadid''s Lyme disease diagnosis during the show''s infamous Munchausen scandal. The arrival of pop-star alter-ego Erika Jayne shifts the show''s aesthetic toward high-camp glam squads, but her narrative takes a severe turn when she becomes embroiled in sprawling, real-world legal and financial scandals. Later seasons prominently feature the eccentric wealth of Dorit Kemsley and Sutton Stracke, as well as the grounded perspective of actress Garcelle Beauvais, who frequently challenges the group''s long-standing cliques.

Throughout its run, the series relies on a formula of minor perceived slights—a misunderstood comment, an unreturned phone call, or a perceived lack of loyalty—escalating into season-long feuds. The women routinely host lavish dinner parties that inevitably descend into tearful screaming matches, only to attempt reconciliation on opulent group holidays to global destinations. Ultimately, the show serves as an extended observation of female friendship, ego, and the extreme lengths to which people will go to protect their public image and social standing in a town where perception is everything.', '["excellent background noise for folding laundry","problems that would instantly vanish if anyone had to do their own chores","dinner parties that make eating alone over the sink look peaceful","grown adults displaying absolutely zero fruit of the spirit"]', 'Returning Series', 'Bravo', 'Diamonds under pressure.', 6.4, 102, '2010-10-14', '2026-03-19', 23.5134, 'en', 'The Real Housewives of Beverly Hills', 'http://www.bravotv.com/the-real-housewives-of-beverly-hills', 328, 15, 1, 'Reality', 'US', '/8ktaCSlCgGDMFzgdYc1LYF6CiWq.jpg', '/xmCue1RQDs1BfrHrJwmCD2ETeEb.jpg', '2026-04-03T16:34:53Z', '2026-04-03T19:40:33Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

A hundred years later, two siblings from the Southern Water Tribe, Katara and Sokka, discover a twelve-year-old boy named Aang frozen in an iceberg along with his flying bison, Appa. They soon realize that Aang is the long-lost Avatar and the last surviving Airbender. Aang learns of the devastation the Fire Nation has wrought in his absence and accepts his destiny to restore balance to the world. However, he must first master the remaining three elements—water, earth, and fire—before the arrival of Sozin''s Comet, a celestial event that will grant the Fire Nation immense power and allow them to permanently conquer the world.

Throughout their journey, Aang, Katara, and Sokka are relentlessly pursued by Prince Zuko, the exiled son of the current Fire Lord, Ozai. Zuko believes capturing the Avatar is the only way to restore his honor and return home, and he is often accompanied by his wise and peaceful uncle, Iroh. As the group travels the globe, they gain new allies, including Toph Beifong, a blind but incredibly powerful Earthbender who joins them to teach Aang earthbending. The conflict deepens as Zuko''s ruthless sister, Princess Azula, joins the hunt, capturing the Earth Kingdom capital of Ba Sing Se and nearly killing Aang.

In the final stages of the war, the heroes launch a desperate invasion of the Fire Nation, which ultimately fails but forces them to regroup and prepare for the comet''s arrival. Zuko, having undergone a profound internal struggle regarding his family''s legacy and his own sense of morality, defects from the Fire Nation to join Aang''s group and teach him firebending. In the climactic finale, as Sozin''s Comet arrives, Aang confronts Fire Lord Ozai. Unwilling to compromise his pacifist Air Nomad beliefs by taking a life, Aang uses the ancient art of energybending to strip Ozai of his firebending abilities, permanently neutralizing the threat. Simultaneously, Zuko and Katara defeat Azula, while Sokka, Toph, and their allies dismantle the Fire Nation''s air fleet. With Ozai defeated, Zuko is crowned the new Fire Lord and declares an end to the Hundred Year War, joining Aang in rebuilding the world and ushering in an era of peace.', '["finding a non-lethal third option when everyone tells you murder is the only way","old men dispensing profound moral wisdom over a hot beverage","children carrying the psychological weight of an entire world war","prodigal sons choosing virtue over a toxic family legacy","siblings who actually love and protect each other"]', 'Ended', 'Nickelodeon', 'Water. Earth. Fire. Air.', 8.755, 4748, '2005-02-21', '2008-07-19', 28.5488, 'en', 'Avatar: The Last Airbender', 'https://www.nick.com/shows/avatar-the-last-airbender', 61, 3, 0, 'Scripted', 'US', '/9RQhVb3r3mCMqYVhLoCu4EvuipP.jpg', '/kU98MbVVgi72wzceyrEbClZmMFe.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:40:47Z', '2026-04-03T19:40:46Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.homepage, number_of_episodes = excluded.number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons = excluded.number_of_seasons, in_production = excluded.in_production, type = excluded.type, origin_country = excluded.origin_country, poster_key = excluded.poster_key, backdrop_key = excluded.backdrop_key, created_at = excluded.created_at, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

Under the Postman''s watchful eye, Bernard learns that the device comes with strict rules: it must never be used to commit crimes, inflict harm, or fulfill selfish desires. Instead, Bernard uses the watch to arrive at school on time, prevent minor accidents, and quietly resolve the day-to-day dilemmas facing his family and peers. As he grows more responsible with his gift, he occasionally shares his secret with a select few, including his best friend Karen and his cousin Lucy, who assist him in his quiet missions to help others. The original run of the series maintains a gentle episodic focus on childhood problem-solving, with the Postman stepping in occasionally to guide Bernard or lend out other magical watches to those in need.

In the later seasons, the series shifts to a new continuity centered on a slightly older Bernard. In this iteration, the watch simply flies through Bernard''s bedroom window, and he is seemingly the only person in the world to possess such a device. Sharing his secret with his closest friend, Nathan, Bernard navigates the social hierarchies and academic pressures of Pentup Primary School. The overarching storylines of this era focus heavily on Bernard''s ongoing efforts to outwit his tyrannical school teacher, Ms. Yvonne Savage, and to humble his arrogant, popular rival, Nicolette. Whether evading classroom punishments, orchestrating elaborate pranks to thwart bullies, or restoring fairness to schoolyard disputes, Bernard relies on the watch to maintain order and protect his friends, all while keeping the adult world entirely oblivious to his power.', '["the sheer logistical fantasy of pausing time to take a nap","sensible british children patiently managing the adults around them","using supernatural abilities almost entirely for mundane chores","entrusted with cosmic power but mostly using it to avoid being late for school"]', 'Ended', 'CITV', '', 6.3, 6, '1997-11-14', '2005-03-31', 1.9246, 'en', 'Bernard''s Watch', '', 79, 7, 0, 'Scripted', 'GB', '/5bBB7Q3ekDGAqPzprfmpB11aGj0.jpg', '/s0n7MNnBXiskWkPVPhtF3r2FcGK.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:20:03Z', '2026-04-03T19:40:50Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET title = excluded.title, tmdb_id = excluded.tmdb_id, tvdb_id = excluded.tvdb_id, year = excluded.year, overview = excluded.overview, plot = excluded.plot, shelf_suggestions = excluded.shelf_suggestions, status = excluded.status, network = excluded.network, tagline = excluded.tagline, vote_average = excluded.vote_average, vote_count = excluded.vote_count, first_air_date = excluded.first_air_date, last_air_date = excluded.last_air_date, popularity = excluded.popularity, original_language = excluded.original_language, original_name = excluded.original_name, homepage = excluded.